{"nodes": [{"id": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_loop_forms_control_flow_and_choosing_loop_capability_table", "label": "Loop capability table", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/javascript/pages/phase-6-iteration-and-destructuring/loop-forms/control-flow-and-choosing.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If the body needs break, continue, return from the enclosing function, or await, forEach and array methods are out. MDN: no way to stop forEach except throwing."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_loop_forms_control_flow_and_choosing_foreach_return_is_continue", "label": "return inside forEach is continue", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/javascript/pages/phase-6-iteration-and-destructuring/loop-forms/control-flow-and-choosing.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "return exits the callback only. The enclosing function always continues \u2014 a silent compile-clean bug. Use find or for...of."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_loop_forms_control_flow_and_choosing_await_only_in_real_loop", "label": "await only works in a real loop", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/javascript/pages/phase-6-iteration-and-destructuring/loop-forms/control-flow-and-choosing.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "forEach discards async callback promises: work is not awaited and rejections are unhandled. for...of+await is sequential; Promise.all+map is concurrent."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_loop_forms_control_flow_and_choosing_sequential_vs_concurrent", "label": "Sequential for...of vs Promise.all", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/javascript/pages/phase-6-iteration-and-destructuring/loop-forms/control-flow-and-choosing.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "for...of+await when operations depend on each other or the target cannot take parallel load. Promise.all starts every request at once."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_loop_forms_control_flow_and_choosing_labeled_break", "label": "Labeled break for nested loops", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/javascript/pages/phase-6-iteration-and-destructuring/loop-forms/control-flow-and-choosing.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "break/continue accept a label to exit two loops. Only works with real loops, not forEach. Extracting to a function and return is often cleaner."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_loop_forms_control_flow_and_choosing_for_of_live_iterator", "label": "for...of live iterator vs forEach snapshot", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/javascript/pages/phase-6-iteration-and-destructuring/loop-forms/control-flow-and-choosing.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "forEach fixes its range before the first callback. for...of re-reads length, so push during iteration over the same array is an infinite loop."}], "edges": [{"source": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_loop_forms_control_flow_and_choosing_loop_capability_table", "target": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_loop_forms_what_each_iterates_foreach", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "sour